  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Defend as a team",
  "description": "Play 8 v 8 on half the rink towards one goal with a keeper. The coach stands at the centre spot with balls and starts every attack with a pass to blue, who attack and try to score. Offside applies. A ball over the boards gives a stroke-in; a ball over the end line means the next attack starts with the coach.\n\nRed defend in two lines of four: a back line with the defenders and a front line with the midfielders. If red win the ball they score by playing it back to the coach, making three passes in a row, or skating with the ball under control over the halfway line.\n\nStop the game when needed and show the distances within and between the lines – things happen fast on ice and a gap soon becomes a breakaway. Swap roles after 8–10 minutes. The diagram does not show every blue player and is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep good distances within and between the lines – no gaps to play the ball through."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The nearest player skates out and presses, the others shift with the ball and cover."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Step up together when the ball is played backwards or out to the boards – keep the offside line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Keeper and defenders talk all the time – who takes whom, when do we step up?"
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
